# REST Service

`@furystack/eslint-plugin` enforces most patterns — generate compliant code from the start.

## Layered model — per-module split

```
common/src/apis/<module>.ts                    ← per-module RestApi-derived interface
common/src/apis/index.ts                       ← aggregate re-exports
common/schemas/*.json                          ← generated by yarn create-schemas
service/src/app-models/<module>/
  ├── setup-<module>-rest-api.ts               ← per-module endpoint registration
  └── setup-<module>-store.ts                  ← per-module stores + DataSets
service/src/service.ts                         ← composes all setup-*-rest-api calls
service/src/setup-entity-sync.ts               ← entity sync wiring
```

Frontend imports the per-module API from `common` and gets typed calls automatically through the API client.

## API contract per module

```typescript
// common/src/apis/services.ts
import type { RestApi } from '@furystack/rest'
import type { Service } from '../models/service.js'

export type GetServiceEndpoint = { url: { id: string }; result: Service }
export type StartServiceEndpoint = { url: { id: string }; result: { pid: number } }

export interface ServicesApi extends RestApi {
  GET: { '/services/:id': GetServiceEndpoint }
  POST: { '/services/:id/start': StartServiceEndpoint }
}
```

Re-export from `common/src/apis/index.ts`. Re-run `yarn create-schemas` after changing API types to refresh `common/schemas/*.json`.

## Endpoint registration per module

```typescript
// service/src/app-models/services/setup-services-rest-api.ts
import {
  Authenticate,
  JsonResult,
  Validate,
  createGetEntityEndpoint,
  useRestService,
} from '@furystack/rest-service'
import type { ServicesApi } from 'common'
import StackCraftSchemas from 'common/schemas/stackcraft.json' with { type: 'json' }

export const setupServicesRestApi = async (injector: Injector): Promise<void> => {
  await useRestService<ServicesApi>({
    injector,
    root: 'api/services',
    api: {
      GET: {
        '/services/:id': Authenticate()(createGetEntityEndpoint(ServiceDataSet)),
      },
      POST: {
        '/services/:id/start': Authenticate()(
          Validate({ schema: StackCraftSchemas, schemaName: 'StartServiceEndpoint' })(
            async (options) => {
              const { id } = options.getUrlParams()
              const pid = await injector.get(ProcessManager).start(id)
              return JsonResult({ pid })
            },
          ),
        ),
      },
    },
  })
}
```

`service/src/service.ts` composes all per-module setups in sequence inside the `setupRestApis()` function.

## Validation

`furystack/rest-action-validate-wrapper` requires `Validate({ schema, schemaName })` around custom actions that consume `query`, `url`, or `body`. Built-in framework actions handle their own validation — those are an explicit lint exception with a justification comment.

## Errors

Throw `RequestError(message, code)`. Plain `throw new Error(...)` in REST actions is forbidden by `rest-action-use-request-error`.

| Code | Meaning |
|---|---|
| 400 | Validation / bad input |
| 401 | Unauthenticated |
| 403 | Forbidden (authorized but not permitted) |
| 404 | Not found |
| 409 | Conflict (duplicate, version mismatch) |
| 500 | Server error |

```typescript
import { RequestError } from '@furystack/rest-service'

if (!service) throw new RequestError('Service not found', 404)
if (alreadyRunning) throw new RequestError('Service already running', 409)
```

## Authentication

`useHttpAuthentication` + optional `useJwtAuthentication` wired in `service/src/config.ts`. Wrap auth-required custom endpoints with `Authenticate()`. JWT login / refresh / logout actions are built-in (`createJwtLoginAction(injector)`, `JwtRefreshAction`, `JwtLogoutAction`).

## Stores + DataSets

Use `defineStore`, `defineFileSystemStore`, `defineSequelizeStore`, `defineDataSet`. Bind framework throw-by-default tokens (`UserStore`, `SessionStore`, `PasswordCredentialStore`, `RefreshTokenStore`) to your concrete stores in `setup-<module>-store.ts`.

```typescript
import { defineStore, InMemoryStore } from '@furystack/core'
import { defineDataSet } from '@furystack/repository'

const ServicesStore = defineStore({
  name: 'app/ServicesStore',
  model: Service,
  primaryKey: 'id',
  factory: () => new InMemoryStore({ model: Service, primaryKey: 'id' }),
})

export const ServiceDataSet = defineDataSet({
  name: 'app/ServiceDataSet',
  store: ServicesStore,
  settings: { ...authorizedDataSet, /* hooks */ },
})
```

## DataSet over StoreToken in app code

`furystack/no-direct-store-token` enforces resolving the **DataSet token** (or `getDataSetFor`) from app code. Direct `injector.get(<Store>)` in a REST action bypasses authorization, hooks, and entity sync.

Allowed direct-store-token uses: store implementations, inside DataSet factories, test data seeding.

## Entity sync

`service/src/setup-entity-sync.ts` registers DataSets for cross-frontend cache invalidation:

```typescript
import { useEntitySync } from '@furystack/rest-service'

export const setupEntitySync = (injector: Injector): void => {
  useEntitySync(injector, { models: [ServiceDataSet, StackDataSet, /* ... */] })
}
```

Each entry must be a `DataSetToken`, not a raw store token.

## CORS

Configured per environment in `service/src/get-cors-options.ts`. Apply via the `cors` option of `useRestService`.

## Graceful shutdown

`service/src/shutdown-handler.ts` listens for `SIGTERM` / `SIGINT` and disposes the injector before exit. Don't bypass it.

## Commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `yarn create-schemas` | regenerate `common/schemas/*.json` from API types |
| `yarn start:service` | start the service |
| `yarn build` | typecheck + build |
| `yarn test` | unit tests |
| `yarn test:e2e` | Playwright E2E |
